{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14031 - MONDO_20543",
  "verbalization": "Tretamine, a compound with a well-documented indication for Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, appears to be linked to Theca Steroid-producing Cell Malignant Tumor Of Ovary, Not Further Specified through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Tretamine may exert a therapeutic effect on this tumor type by interacting with the malignant germ cell lineage, as indicated by its use in conjunction with Melphalan and Belotecan. The shared indication for Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary across these paths implies a potential mechanism of action that targets this specific tumor type. The presence of a consistent pathway involving Melphalan and Belotecan, both of which are used in the treatment of this tumor, further supports the notion that Tretamine may have a role in modulating the tumor's biological behavior. The integrated evidence suggests that Tretamine could potentially be a candidate for repositioning in the treatment of Theca Steroid-producing Cell Malignant Tumor Of Ovary, Not Further Specified, provided additional mechanistic validation is obtained.",
